{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>לכן נאום</b> [Therefore, an utterance]. It is a noun, like וינאמו נאום [and they uttered an utterance]. And one who says נם instead of נאם — it is נם, for the alef is not elided." "And the sense of <b>האדון</b> [the Master] is on account of the judges, for they are the masters of the land." "And the sense of <b>יי צבאות</b> [YHWH of hosts] — that He is truly the Master, and the hosts are witnesses. And why the Name is joined to צבאות [hosts] is explained in Samuel." "<b>אביר ישראל</b> [Mighty One of Israel]. For they are in the camp like a host on high, for they too are called the hosts of HaShem, as written in the Torah (Exodus 12:41)." "<b>הוי</b> [Hoy]. Like 'woe to them' when I do thus." "<b>אנחם</b> [I will comfort them]. I will find consolation, for they provoked me — in the manner of human speech."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:36.289737070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}